\paragraph{Claim-clustered intervals on H1 (descriptive, post-hoc).} The accuracies above are point estimates over hundreds of graded trials, and \textbf{the trials are nested}: the unit is the paired claim, 12--23 of them per target, not the 231--400 trials (Table~\ref{tab:inference_ladder}). A cluster bootstrap over claims on the \emph{same} estimator (2{,}000 draws, seed~42, each draw resampling that cell's distinct claims with replacement and giving each drawn copy a fresh group id) gives, in table order, 95\% accuracy intervals $[0.827,0.936]$, $[0.794,0.918]$, $[0.525,0.795]$, $[0.793,0.924]$ and $[0.692,0.843]$. \textbf{An accuracy interval alone would mislead here}, because resampling claims moves the $D$ base rate and the estimator's own majority baseline moves with it, so we also report the interval on \textbf{accuracy minus that draw's own baseline}: $[+0.172,+0.400]$ and $[+0.181,+0.382]$ on the two replicated positives, against $[-0.078,+0.105]$, $[-0.011,+0.095]$ and $[-0.031,+0.089]$ on the other three. Family~E behaves the same way, Mistral-Nemo~12B at $[+0.092,+0.329]$ and the other four straddling zero (the widest is OLMo~2~13B, accuracy $[0.468,0.800]$). \textbf{This is descriptive and it is not a second test}: the pre-registered inference is the within-claim permutation test corrected within each family, and the fact that the margin excludes zero on exactly the three cells committed as positive and on no other cell is a statistic agreeing with that test rather than evidence added to it. \textbf{What stays thin is the count, not the cells}: at the claim level each positive cell is estimated tightly enough to be read, and the fragile quantity is \textbf{one of five} targets, exact 95\% interval $[0.005,\,0.716]$. Computed by \texttt{experiments/analyze\_crit4b\_ci.py}, which recomputes every cell's point accuracy from the committed candidate rows and asserts it equals the published value before reporting any interval; \textbf{no number in Table~\ref{tab:crit4b_h1} changes}, and the arm is logged as post-hoc in the pre-registration's §12(17).
